      "overall_weighted_score_10": 7.97,
      "synthesis_summary": "[Derived] Apple scores in the top tier on Moat (9.4) and Financials (9.4) due to extraordinary profitability and balance sheet fortitude, balanced downward by a moderate Valuation score (4.8) and mid-tier Growth score (6.8), producing a composite rating of 7.97/10."
    },
    "SECTION_17_GLOSSARY": {
      "terms": [
        {
          "term": "Altman Z-Score",
          "definition": "A formula combining five financial ratios to evaluate the probability of bankruptcy; scores above 3.0 designate the Safe Zone."
        },
        {
          "term": "Beneish M-Score",
          "definition": "A mathematical model using eight financial ratios to identify whether a company has manipulated its reported earnings; scores below -1.78 indicate non-manipulator status."
        },
        {
          "term": "Economic Moat",
          "definition": "A company's competitive advantage that shields its market share and structural long-term profits from competitors."
        },
        {
          "term": "ROIC (Return on Invested Capital)",
          "definition": "A profitability ratio calculating how efficiently a company allocates capital to generate profits relative to its invested debt and equity base."
        },
        {
          "term": "FCF Yield",
          "definition": "Free cash flow per share divided by the current share price, measuring the percentage of actual cash generated relative to enterprise equity valuation."
        }
      ]
    },
    "SECTION_18_LAY_SUMMARY": {
      "summary": "[Judgment] Apple designs popular consumer electronics (iPhone, Mac, iPad, Watch) and runs the digital services integrated into them (App Store, iCloud, Apple Pay). Because customers rarely abandon the Apple platform once they own multiple devices, Apple enjoys high customer loyalty and strong profits. While the business is financially strong with little bankruptcy risk, its stock is currently priced at a high level relative to expected single-digit profit growth."
    }
  }
